{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospitalists. You're here for your eighth cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your CNS lymphoma, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. I hope this one goes as smoothly as the last."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best. I see your history includes ulcerative colitis, asthma, and that you’re on enoxaparin for a prior DVT and PE. Any new symptoms since your last admission?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fevers or breathing issues. But my right foot pain flared up this weekend after I walked more than usual. It’s that same burning feeling going up my leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We’ve checked with MRI, ultrasound, and even a lumbar puncture before—all normal. We still think it’s likely neuropathic. We’ll keep you on gabapentin and adjust if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief it’s not something new. But it really limits how much I can stand or walk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll monitor it closely. Now, we’ll start your chemotherapy today. You’ll get high-dose methotrexate, and we’ll use sodium bicarbonate in your IV fluids to help protect your kidneys and help clear the drug."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, and I remember we have to keep my urine alkaline. That’s why I take those bicarb pills sometimes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll give you oral bicarbonate if needed to keep your urine pH above 7.5. We’ll check it regularly. You’ll also get leucovorin starting 24 hours after the chemo to reduce side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the anti-nausea meds? I usually feel queasy after the first dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve scheduled ondansetron regularly, and we can give extra if needed. We also have ativan and compazine available. We’ll keep you comfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And my ulcerative colitis meds—I’m not taking mesalamine right now, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. We hold mesalamine during methotrexate because it can increase toxicity. You’ll restart it when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my port was placed yesterday—I saw the X-ray confirmed it’s in the right spot?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-08-04 10:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the chest X-ray this morning shows your Port-A-Cath is in good position in the SVC. The PICC line is out, so we’ll use the port for all your infusions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-08-04 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start the methotrexate infusion. Any questions before we begin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-08-04 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready. Just let me know if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-08-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the infusion. We’re continuing with bicarbonate IV fluids. Your urine pH is at 7.8 now—perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-08-04 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I feel a little nauseated, but not bad yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-08-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll order a dose of ondansetron to stay ahead of it. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-08-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your first methotrexate level came back at 24 hours—0.92. That’s expected. We’ve started your leucovorin rescue—every six hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-08-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that level safe? I remember last time it dropped quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-08-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s on track. We’ll check again tomorrow. Your kidney function is excellent—creatinine clearance is 135 mL/min—so we expect it to clear well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-08-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My foot pain is a bit better today—maybe from resting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-08-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll keep your gabapentin going and add oxycodone if it flares again. We’re also watching your potassium and phosphate—IV fluids can lower them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-08-05 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show mild hypokalemia and hypophosphatemia. We’re giving potassium IV and phosphate by mouth. It should correct quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-08-05 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? I’ve heard low potassium can affect the heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-08-05 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We caught it early. Your EKG is normal, and we’re replacing it steadily. No risk at this level."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-08-06 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your methotrexate level is down to 0.21. That’s a great drop. We’ll keep leucovorin and fluids going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-08-06 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m on track to go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-08-06 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if your next level is below 0.10, you won’t need to take leucovorin or bicarbonate at home. We’ll check it this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-08-06 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I hate taking so many pills after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-08-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your level is 0.13 this morning. We’ll keep IV leucovorin and fluids a few more hours. It should drop below 0.10 by this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-08-06 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll still be here for a bit longer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-08-06 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, just until we confirm safe clearance. We don’t want to risk methotrexate toxicity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-08-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Nausea is gone, and your headache from yesterday is better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-08-06 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the acetaminophen helped. I think it was from the zofran or the chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-08-06 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possible. We’ll keep it on hand if it comes back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-08-07 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level this morning is 0.13, but since you’ve been on leucovorin and fluids, it should be under 0.10 by noon. We’re planning discharge around 1 PM."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-08-07 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Will I need to take anything special at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-08-07 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No leucovorin or bicarbonate this time—your levels cleared well. Just your regular meds: gabapentin, enoxaparin, your asthma inhalers, and restart mesalamine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-08-07 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the foot pain—should I see a neurologist or get another MRI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-08-07 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll consider an MRI of the foot and repeat lumbar spine MRI soon. For now, keep using gabapentin and PRN pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-08-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Potassium and phosphate are normal now. Liver enzymes are slightly elevated, as usual with chemo, but nothing concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-08-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the transaminitis is expected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-08-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it happens every cycle. We may increase leucovorin next time to help protect your liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final update: your methotrexate level dropped below 0.10. You’re cleared to go home without oral leucovorin or bicarbonate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When do I come back for the next cycle?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In two weeks. You’ll have another MRI during that admission to check your brain lesion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my enoxaparin—I keep that going the whole time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue twice daily. No changes there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did great. Rest up, restart your mesalamine, and we’ll see you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I get the same anti-nausea meds next time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, same regimen. We can adjust if needed, but what we’re doing seems to be working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. And my headache—is it safe to use oxycodone if it comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it can make nausea worse. Try acetaminophen first. Use oxycodone only if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-08-07 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if you have fever, severe pain, or trouble breathing. Otherwise, see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you’re feeling well enough to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m ready. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications. You’re cleared to leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well in your treatment. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2175-08-07 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-08-04 10:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-08-07 13:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her eighth cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well, with expected mild transaminitis and stable mild anemia. Her methotrexate levels cleared appropriately, allowing for IV leucovorin rescue without the need for oral leucovorin or bicarbonate at discharge. Chronic right foot pain, likely neuropathic, persisted but was managed with gabapentin and PRN analgesics. She remained neurologically stable, with plans for a repeat MRI during her next admission. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to restart mesalamine, continue enoxaparin, and return in two weeks for her next chemotherapy cycle.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Transaminitis (abnormal liver function tests)",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Disorders of phosphorus metabolism",
      "Anemia in neoplastic disease",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Multiple sclerosis",
      "Headache"
    ]
  }
}
